a) Normalization in MSstats is for removing any systematic variation. and Normalization is performed with all features, which means before selecting top N or removing uninformative features. The same normalization will be performed whether you select either top 5 or top 10 features.

b) previous version (before v3.18.1) : data was correctly imputed and estimated log 2 protein intensity was correct. The only values in NumImputedFeature column were reported wrongly. Now, v3.18.1 is available from Bioconductor 3.10, which corrected this reporting issue.

- Meena

